<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">appearance</ansi>

How you look, in your own words: your age, height, build, face, skin,
hair, and any marks. Others read it when they <ansi fg="command">look</ansi> at you.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Commands</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">appearance</ansi>          shows how you look and what you chose
  <ansi fg="command">appearance edit</ansi>     chooses your looks again (at an inn only)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Choosing</ansi>

You choose your looks when you make a character, one short question at a
time, and see the description build as you go. A last line of your own
(up to 160 characters) is optional. Looks are only words: they change no
numbers and never help or hurt you in a fight.

In the web client the questions open as a panel of buttons, with your
figure drawn in the skin and hair you chose. Type the same number or word
at the game line if you prefer; "Type instead" tucks the panel away.
<ansi fg="command">back</ansi> starts your looks over, and <ansi fg="command">cancel</ansi> leaves <ansi fg="command">appearance edit</ansi>
with nothing changed.

Your chosen skin and hair show on the battle screen and in that panel.
The figures on the world map are newly painted and do not show them yet;
there you appear in your class's own colours.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Changing them</ansi>

At any inn, <ansi fg="command">appearance edit</ansi> lets you choose again. It is free, as often as
you like. Your life story stays as it was (<ansi fg="command">help lifestory</ansi>).

Your pronouns are part of your looks. Your description and your life
story are written with them.

Characters made before looks existed are asked once, when they next log
in. You may skip it, and ask later with <ansi fg="command">creation</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help lifestory</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help archetype</ansi>.
